<%# Says how far a "Search transcript contents" search actually got.

    Transcript search is bounded (SessionContentSearch): it walks sessions newest-first
    and stops at its result cap or its time budget, so an empty result is not the same
    claim as "there is no such session". Saying which one happened is the whole point —
    the unbounded version of this query returned a gateway timeout instead. %>
<% if scan %>
  <div class="mb-4 rounded-md border px-3 py-2 text-xs <%= scan.complete? ? "border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 text-gray-600" : "border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 text-amber-800" %>">
    <% if scan.complete? %>
      Transcript scan complete — all <%= number_with_delimiter(scan.candidate_count) %>
      <%= "session".pluralize(scan.candidate_count) %> matching these filters were searched.
    <% else %>
      Transcript scan stopped early: the newest
      <%= number_with_delimiter(scan.scanned) %> of
      <%= number_with_delimiter(scan.candidate_count) %> matching
      <%= "session".pluralize(scan.candidate_count) %> were searched
      <%= scan.timed_out? ? "before the time budget ran out" : "before the result limit was reached" %>.
      Older sessions have not been ruled out — narrow the status, genesis or agent-root
      filters to reach further back.
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
